//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Kassahi 3-star / 4-star unique decoration rules (Phil777; the Kassahi bucket
// uses 19-Kassahi_UNID-stars[ONLY=KassahiStd,...], whose aliases carry the sound)
//
// Restores the upstream Kassahi project's icon/sound prefix on top of the alias
// references. Hiim's shared 20-Unid_UniquesSet_Tiers[ALL].filter drops the
// %DOT-0D%%MAP-21%%BORDER-0A% / %PX-0D%%DOT-21%%MAP-0A% decoration and uses a
// different 3-star sound (4726 vs upstream 4714); for ETH copies rated below their
// non-ETH copy it tiers down instead of using %BLAME_ONION%.
//
// FILTLVL gating preserved (per project policy). Numbered 00- to fire before the
// shared 20- rules.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// 4-star unique (non-ETH and ETH copies are tiered separately)
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID !ETH FILTLVL<11 4_STAR_UNIQUE]: %UNI_GG_ITEM%%FX_UNID_GG%
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID ETH FILTLVL<11 4_STAR_ETH_UNIQUE]: %UNI_GG_ITEM%%FX_UNID_GG%
// ETH copy of a 4-star base that is rated lower when ETH: blame onion
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID ETH FILTLVL<11 4_STAR_UNIQUE !4_STAR_ETH_UNIQUE]: %BLAME_ONION%

// 3-star unique
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID !ETH FILTLVL<9 3_STAR_UNIQUE]: %UNI_STAR3_ITEM%%FX_STARS_3%
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID ETH FILTLVL<9 3_STAR_ETH_UNIQUE]: %UNI_STAR3_ITEM%%FX_STARS_3%
// ETH copy of a 3-star base that is rated lower when ETH: blame onion
ItemDisplay[UNI !ID ETH FILTLVL<9 3_STAR_UNIQUE !3_STAR_ETH_UNIQUE]: %BLAME_ONION%
